From 11e1762d93930a6643b0f6c499b5bc9055a3b321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:09:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06918/11362] [outer-loop] dc22: L6 SOLVED, FULL GAME CLEAR
 (round 10, codex)

Round-10 gpt-5.6-sol session executed round 9's corrected route via
pure live play, and it worked exactly as predicted -- confirming the
polymorphic latch mechanism live for the first time. Driving the bare
C-structure four control positions left and clicking the wide 8-bar
latched the long bridge instead of the 8-ring (a 48-cell live frame
diff). Transported it via the known D-pad path, retyped LM to C/B,
routed to R1's checker, then DOWN2/EAST14/NORTH1/EAST7 reached the
goal. levels_completed advanced to 6 with GameState.WIN.

The source agent's own fresh-environment reproduction gate confirmed
the same result independently. The outer loop independently
re-verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay, all 5 confirmed
level=6, state=GameState.WIN. L6 is dc22's final level -- the game is
fully solved, closing the longest-running open frontier of this entire
breadth campaign (10 rounds).

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: dc22 levels_reproduced 5 -> 6,
full_game_clear: true, final_game_state: GameState.WIN.
reproducible_total_levels 166 -> 167 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
